    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\n`vim.lsp.document_color` errors when a server returns a color with a component outside the LSP range of 0-1 \n\n- for example a negative value for an out-of-gamut color\n- The whole documentColor response is dropped, so no colors from that response are shown.\n\n<img width=\"1238\" height=\"895\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0fde57d4-3f75-490c-b4be-c464249889cf\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n### minimal init.lua\n```lua\nvim.pack.add({ \"https://github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig\" }, { confirm = false })\n\nvim.lsp.enable \"css_variables\"\nvim.lsp.document_color.enable(true, nil, { style = \"virtual\" })\n``` \n\n### css file \n\n```css\nbody {\n  color: #ff8000\n}\n\n:root {\n  --bg: oklch(1 0 0);\n  --fg: oklch(0.577 0.245 27.325);\n  --mixed: color-mix(in oklab, var(--fg) 10%, var(--bg));\n}\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nClamp the components to 0-1, or skip the invalid color, instead of throwing.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1952+g187d13aa60)\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\ndidnt try vim!\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nGnu/Void Linux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nst\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nst-256\n\n### Installation\n\npkg manager",
